# Line-ending policy for the whole repository.
#
# Git stores every text file normalized to LF in the repository (the committed blob),
# and checks it out with CRLF (\r\n) line endings in the working tree on every machine.
# Result: files on disk are always CRLF (Windows style), while the stored/shared form is
# a uniform LF, so diffs never show spurious whole-file line-ending changes again.
#
# `text=auto` lets git auto-detect text vs binary by content; binary files are left
# untouched. A developer who wants LF on their own disk can override locally (and only
# for their clone) via .git/info/attributes with `* text=auto eol=lf`.
* text=auto eol=crlf

# Be explicit about binary assets so they are never treated as text / line-ending converted.
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf  binary
*.jar  binary
